<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dotawo</h1><p class="st-meta">1365 CE – 1484 CE (approx.) · capital Gebel Adda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Christian Nubian kingdom on the Nile, a rump of Makuria centred at Gebel Adda and Qasr Ibrim that survived into the late 15th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dotawo was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-nubian">Old Nubian</a> name used in documents for the realm of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/makuria">Makuria</a>. After Dongola was abandoned around 1365 amid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> interventions and Arab raids, the surviving court moved north to Daw, generally identified with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebel-adda">Gebel Adda</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a>, and the reduced kingdom is known by this name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom is known mainly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-nubian">Old Nubian</a> letters and legal documents found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qasr-ibrim">Qasr Ibrim</a> and from scattered Arabic notices. It kept the Nubian Church with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, Greek and Old Nubian liturgy, and a court with eparchs and officials in the tradition of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/makuria">Makuria</a>, but its territory and resources were small.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The last known king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joel-of-dotawo">Joel</a>, is attested in 1484. Dotawo then disappears from the record, probably absorbed during the spread of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and Arab tribes and the rise of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/funj-sultanate">Funj Sultanate</a>, which ended Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1365 CE – 1484 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.87%;width:2.37%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1365 CE – 1484 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gebel Adda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Joel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity (Nubian Church)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Nubian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dotawo, Daw</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1424&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dotawo" aria-label="Kingdom of Dotawo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5527 1354 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Dotawo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5847 1610L5833 1758"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5833 1758h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5847 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5847 1610h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gebel Adda. <a href="/atlas?year=1424&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dotawo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
